{"5081510": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Paint The World", "steam_appid": 5081510, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "controller_support": "full", "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Everything starts white. The buildings, the streets, the trees, the cars parked at the curb - a whole little town with no color in it. What you do about that is up to you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You point at something and paint the exact spot you're looking at, and the color stays. Simple enough. But paint a tree all the way and it starts swaying in the wind. Paint one of those parked cars and it pulls out and drives off down the street. The fountain runs once you've painted it. Paint the birds sitting on a lamppost and they scatter into the sky. The more of the town you color, the more of it is alive and moving around you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There's no timer and nothing to lose here - paint for ten minutes or a whole evening, whichever you're in the mood for. Every town is built from a seed, so a fresh one is always a click away, and if you'd rather paint something of your own you can load in a .glb and start it blank. It remembers where you left off. Bring a friend and you can paint a town together over your network or via Steam Friends.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >New tools and colors turn up as you play - a roller, a spray can, a bucket, metallic paint, glow paint that actually lights the place up after dark. And there's a quiet soundtrack drifting along behind it that never quite loops.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It's a white world. Go put some color on it!</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Everything starts white. The buildings, the streets, the trees, the cars parked at the curb - a whole little town with no color in it. What you do about that is up to you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You point at something and paint the exact spot you're looking at, and the color stays. Simple enough. But paint 